<td><h2>Dwellop AS – Chairman steps down</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2019-02-22 08:23:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Dwellop’s Chairman Mr. Eirik Bergsvik has been appointed as the new CEO in MH Wirth.  In order to avoid potential conflict of interests, Mr. Bergsvik has voluntarily decided to step down as Chairman of the board of directors of Dwellop, effective immediately.  The board would like to thank Mr. Bergsvik for his contribution and wish him all the best in his future endeavors.   <br><br>Mr. Sigmund Prestegaard, board member of Dwellop, has kindly accepted to function as Chairman of the board of directors of Dwellop until the next General meeting in May 2019. If shareholders controlling more than 10 % of the shares of the company require that a new chairman of the board is appointed immediately, the board of directors will call for an extraordinary general meeting. <br><br>* * *<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>Helge Hustoft, Chief Executive Officer<br>Phone: +47 51 57 29 12<br>Mobile: +47 91 57 58 76<br>E-mail: helge.hustoft@dwellop.no <br>This information is published in accordance with the disclosure requirements set out in the Continuing Obligations for companies with shares registered on the NOTC-List.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Dwellop AS: Contract award</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2018-12-20 09:00:12</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Aker BP has awarded a contract to Dwellop AS for development and delivery of a well intervention solution for the Ula platform. The main activity will be performed in 2019 with delivery in Q2. The contract value is 39 MNOK. <br><br><br>  * * *<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>Helge Hustoft, Chief Executive Officer<br>Phone: +47 51 57 29 12<br>Mobile: +47 91 57 58 76<br>E-mail: helge.hustoft@dwellop.no <br>This information is published in accordance with the disclosure requirements set out in the Continuing Obligations for companies with shares registered on the NOTC-List.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Dwellop AS: Successful outcome of legal proceedings regarding alleged patent infringement</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2018-10-30 08:03:32</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Reference is made to the stock exchange announcement made by Hunter Group ASA (Oslo Axess ticker: "HUNT") on 23 June 2017 regarding the legal proceedings initiated by WellPartner AS ("WellPartner") against Dwellop AS ("Dwellop" or the "Company"). WellPartner's claims were based on an allegation that Dwellop had infringed WellPartner's Norwegian patent NO 336 036 B1 relating to a solution for back-up heave compensation lifting frames. WellPartner claimed i.a. an injunction in respect of Dwellop's Heave Compensated Tension Frame technology and damages/consideration estimated to approximately NOK 8.1 million for the alleged infringement. The legal proceedings were held from 30 August to 6 September 2018 before Oslo District Court. <br><br>Oslo District Court has in its judgment of 26 October 2018 concluded that WellPartner's Norwegian patent NO 336 036 B1 is invalid. On this basis, Oslo District Court has dismissed all of WellPartner's claims against Dwellop, and accordingly Dwellop has won the case in all material respects. WellPartner must also cover all of Dwellop's costs in connection with the legal proceedings.<br><br>* * *<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>Helge Hustoft, Chief Executive Officer<br>Phone: +47 51 57 29 12<br>Mobile: +47 91 57 58 76<br>E-mail: helge.hustoft@dwellop.no <br>This information is published in accordance with the disclosure requirements set out in the Continuing Obligations for companies with shares registered on the NOTC-List.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Dwellop AS: Amicable settlement under contract with ENI  Norge AS</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2018-09-14 16:10:57</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Reference is made to the termination notice received from Eni Norge AS in October 2017 with respect to rental of a tension frame for the Goliat platform, as further described at page 16 in Hunter Group ASA's Q3 2017 report attached to the stock exchange notice published by Hunter Group ASA on 15 November 2018. Following negotiations between the parties relating to payment of outstanding rent, the parties have in an amicable settlement on 12 September 2018 agreed that Eni Norge AS, as fully and final settlement, shall pay NOK 5,142.540 (ex VAT) and NOK 799,881 as default interest to Dwellop AS.<br><br>* * *<br>This information is published in accordance with the disclosure requirements set out in the Continuing Obligations for companies with shares registered on the NOTC-List.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
